  "raw_text": "PLAN \"12-Week Fat Loss & Glycaemic Control Program for Type 2 Diabetes (Metabolic Health Focus)\"\nTYPE workout\nVISIBILITY public\n\nGOALS\n  GOAL primary fat_loss:\n    name \"Fat loss with improved glycaemic control and metabolic health\"\n\nPHASES\n  PHASE \"Phase 1\" (4 weeks):\n    WEEK 1:\n      DAY Monday training 45m \"Full-Body Foundations & Glycaemic Strategy\":\n        warmup:\n          walking 5 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          squat 3x10 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          bench_press 3x10 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          bent_over_row 3x10 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          lat_pulldown 3x10 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          dumbbell_shoulder_press 3x12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          ab_wheel 3x10 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          shoulder_stretch 2 minutes\n    WEEK 2:\n      DAY Monday training 45m \"Progression & Glycaemic Modulation\":\n        warmup:\n          walking 5 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          squat 3x8..12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          incline_press 3x8..12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          dumbbell_row 3x8..12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          cable_pulldown 3x8..12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          lateral_raise 3x12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          planks 3x30 seconds rest 30 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          chest_stretch 2 minutes\n  PHASE \"Phase 2\" (4 weeks):\n    WEEK 1:\n      DAY Monday training 50m \"Hypertrophy Emphasis with Cardio Acceleration\":\n        warmup:\n          jogging 5 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          leg_press 3x10 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          bench_press 3x10 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          leg_curl 3x12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          dumbbell_fly 3x12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          seated_row 3x10 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          farmer_walk 2x30 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          hamstring_stretch 2 minutes\n    WEEK 2:\n      DAY Monday training 50m \"Fat-Burning Circuit x Cardio Finisher\":\n        warmup:\n          cycling 5 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          goblet_squat 3x12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          push_up 3x12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          deadlift 3x8 rpe 7 rest 90 seconds\n          overhead_press 3x12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          cable_row 3x12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          jump_rope 1x60 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          calf_raise 2 minutes\n  PHASE \"Phase 3\" (4 weeks):\n    WEEK 1:\n      DAY Monday training 55m \"Conditioning & Diabetes-Focused Adaptations\":\n        warmup:\n          walking 5 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          squat 4x8 rpe 7 rest 75 seconds\n          incline_press 4x8 rpe 7 rest 75 seconds\n          barbell_row 3x10 rpe 7 rest 75 seconds\n          lat_pulldown 3x10 rpe 7 rest 75 seconds\n          face_pull 3x15 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          spine_stretch 2 minutes\n    WEEK 2:\n      DAY Monday training 55m \"Volume & Glycemic Synergy\":\n        warmup:\n          rowing 5 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          leg_extension 3x12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          chest_press 3x12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          leg_curl 3x12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          dumbbell_row 3x12 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          plank 3x40 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          hip_flexor_stretch 2 minutes\n\nNUTRITION STRATEGY (diabetes-aware, designed to pair with training plan)\n- Calorie target: moderate deficit of ~500 kcal/day from estimated maintenance; adjust weekly based on weight trend (aim ~0.5–1.0 kg fat loss/week). Reassess every 4 weeks.\n- Macronutrient distribution (daily, adjustable):\n  - Protein: 1.6–2.0 g/kg bodyweight (to support lean mass and satiety)\n  - Carbohydrates: 2.5–3.0 g/kg bodyweight (adjust for glycemic response; emphasize low-EDGI sources)\n  - Fat: remaining calories; prioritize unsaturated fats\n- Carbohydrate guidelines (diabetes-sensitive):\n  - distribute evenly across meals and workouts\n  - prefer complex carbs: whole grains, legumes, vegetables, fruits with fiber\n  - target 25–40 g fiber/day from vegetables, fruits, whole grains, legumes\n  - monitor postprandial responses; consider a small, balanced carb portion before training if needed\n- Meal timing and structure:\n  - 3 main meals + 1–2 small snacks if needed to meet protein target\n  - pre-workout snack 1–2 hours before training if training intensity >60 minutes or if fasting glucose is high; options: small apple with 1–2 tbsp peanut butter; Greek yogurt with berries\n  - post-workout protein + carb within 2 hours: e.g., whey or plant-based protein + fruit or rice cakes\n- Glycemic targets (general):\n  - fasting glucose: target 90–130 mg/dL\n  - pre-meal: 90–130 mg/dL\n  - post-meal: <180 mg/dL 2 hours after start of meal\n- Metformin considerations:\n  - consistent meal times with medication; avoid very high-fat meals around dosing causing GI upset\n  - hydration and B12 awareness (per clinician guidance)\n- Hydration:\n  - 30–35 ml/kg bodyweight daily; add extra around workouts\n- Supplements (as advised by clinician):\n  - vitamin D if deficient\n  - magnesium/potassium as needed for balance (within medical guidance)\n- Monitoring:\n  - weekly weigh-ins; biweekly body composition if possible\n  - 3–4 day food diary every 2 weeks; review for adherence and carbohydrate distribution\n  - glucometer logs: fasted, pre/post meals, and post-workout readings; adjust nutrition plan with clinician if persistent hyper/hypoglycemia\n- Safety cues:\n  - watch for signs of hypoglycemia during first weeks; carry a quick-acting carb source\n  - adjust carbohydrate portions on days with high-intensity sessions or longer durations\n\nDIABETES-SENSITIVE TRAINING NOTES\n- Start with lower volume and build gradually to reduce risk of hypoglycemia and ensure adherence.\n- Emphasize resistance training for 2–3 days/week and include 1–2 cardio sessions (walking, cycling, rowing) as tolerable, aiming for 150–200 minutes/week gradually.\n- Warmups include light cardio; cooldowns include flexibility work.\n- Monitor RPE to keep sessions sustainable; RPE 6–7 in early weeks, progressing to 7–8 as fitness improves.\n- Adjust rest between sets to maintain safety and hydration.\n\nOUTPUT SPECIFICS\n- All exercises use canonical names from the vocabulary.\n- Rep ranges use two dots (e.g., 3x8..12).\n- Sets come first; rpe follows; rest in seconds after that.\n- Cardio modalities used only from allowed list for warmups/cooldowns and cardio sessions.\n\nNote: Nutrition section is included as explicit guidelines within the plan; employees should coordinate with a registered dietitian or clinician for personalized medication adjustments and lab monitoring.",
